@page "/lazy-load"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Lazy Load</PageTitle>

<h1>Lazy Load</h1>

<p>Trace of the <em>lazy-load</em> example from <code>HtmlFlow-Datastar-Examples</code>.
    In BRHC, deferred content arrives over SSE (<code>data-init="@@get('/lazy-load/graph')"</code>) -
    the server waits 2 seconds and emits <code>patchElements</code> with the image/chart. Here the
    content is loaded in the component's <code>OnInitializedAsync</code> with an equivalent delay.
    <strong>Teaching note:</strong> BRHC's "lazy" is the server pushing later; Blazor's "lazy" is the
    component lifecycle completing later - the transport is invisible.
</p>

<div class="demo-box">
    @if (!loaded)
    {
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <div class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm" role="status"></div>
            <em>Loading deferred content (2s)</em>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="p-4 border rounded bg-light text-center">
            <strong>Heavy content loaded</strong>
            <p class="mb-0 text-muted">(no BRHC este bloco chegou via patchElements no SSE)</p>
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private bool loaded;

    // Equivalent to data-init @@get('/lazy-load/graph') + patchElements after 2s on the server.
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await Task.Delay(2000);
        loaded = true;
    }
}